# live_screen_matches_oracle's own script: captures the live window's drawn HUD and
# construction-menu chrome for a pixel-exact diff against the oracle (tools/ui_layout.py
# compose_screen), the same way ui_mock_compare.py already checks the standalone CPU composer.
# Also switches to the "roads" category (click_px 782 373: category_column_x, construction.txt's
# own "roads" y 373) so a second category's own grid/thumbnails are proven live, not only
# "public" (W4-UI-2's own category-switching checkpoint).
resize 1024 768
wait frames 5
look 1140 516
screenshot hud_idle_live
key b
wait frames 5
screenshot construction_public_live
click_px 782 373
wait frames 5
screenshot construction_roads_live
quit
